        "body": "Dell Technologies is a public company, traded as DELL, that was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Round Rock, Texas. Its site describes it as a provider of technology solutions, services and support, selling laptops, touch screen PCs, desktops, servers, storage, monitors, gaming hardware and accessories. The company's SEC filing identifier is 0001571996.\n\nThe site currently promotes a student offer starting from $599, contingent on purchase of an eligible XPS model DX13260. The offer runs until 11/2/26 at 7am CST and is open to high school students 16 and older and college students at degree granting schools, who must join Dell Rewards or already be members and verify student status. Dell Rewards terms and conditions apply, with a purchase limit of 2 discounted items per order and 2 orders per student per year. Exclusions listed include limited quantity deal order codes, clearance offers, warranties, gift cards and other select PCs.\n\nDell's litigation exposure is recorded in Texas, with a count of 111.",
